---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../site";
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="Which retailer programs are verified, and that links are off in this build." crumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Affiliate disclosure", href: "/disclosure/" }]}>
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
  <p>
    Affiliate links are turned {siteConfig.affiliatesEnabled ? "on" : "off"} in this build.
    While they are off, pages do not carry retailer tracking links.
  </p>
  <p>
    Amazon Associates is a verified program: the standard commission table lists 3% for Lawn and Garden, Tools, and Outdoors, with a 24-hour session.
    Titan Attachments states an Impact program and a 30-day cookie, and the same page states both 4% and 5%. The rate is not settled, so Titan links stay off with the rest.
    Tractor Supply’s public page names Partnerize and does not state a rate. That program is not linked.
  </p>
  <p>
    If links are enabled later, a paid link will be marked with rel sponsored and nofollow, and this page will still say that a commission may be earned.
    Specs will still come from the manufacturer documents, not from the retailer.
  </p>
</Base>
